{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqn469b34mm","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"Graph loop owner is missing","summary":"Foreground/session loops are the only path that drives normal ready-task dispatch today: /loop/status can be empty while the graph has ready tasks, and /next-action only iterates existing active loop records. The daemon headless drain runner is default-on but intentionally scoped to maintenance drains (judge/label/learner), not generic implementation dispatch. Best forward path is to add a daemon-owned, per-workspace graph loop/watchdog so at most one managed background loop exists per graph independent of foreground sessions; keep maintenance drains separate and add tests for empty registry + ready regular work, standing-drain-only graphs, and no duplicate managed loop creation.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-21T01:34:43.359Z","vec":null,"vecs":null,"actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-21T01:34:43.747Z"}
